@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
title Tutorial 1 · Resource states: one synthetic Card
top to bottom direction
skinparam roundcorner 18
hide empty description
state "No owned Card\nCaller has no destruction obligation" as absent
state "Live Card\nCaller holds one destruction obligation" as live
state "destroy_card is active\nCallee has taken the obligation at entry" as destroying
state "Destroyed Card\nObligation discharged; owner lifetime ended" as dead
absent -[bold]-> absent : create_card returns null: valid failure, no obligation
absent -[bold]-> live : create_card returns non-null: valid success, owned Card
live -[bold]-> destroying : destroy_card consumes the owned Card at entry
destroying -[bold]-> dead : destruction ends the lifetime before return
legend bottom
  Rounded box = resource/obligation state; bold arrow = labelled state transition.
  Self-loop preserves the obligation state; arrows are not runtime messages.
  Both creation results are valid to inspect. Null gives nothing to destroy.
  Non-normative: C2, C3, C5. Synthetic lifetime subset; label borrows omitted.
  Listed completions do not promise eventual return.
endlegend
@enduml
